Use execute_program({code}) when many tool calls, deterministic multi-step work, or large results can be filtered in one JavaScript program. For a small simple operation or when you need to reason over each result, call the business tool directly.
Program code is an async function body in an isolated JavaScript sandbox. There is no require, process, fs, or direct workspace access: read files through tools.read_file. Call tools[toolId](input) and inspect {observation, sourceReferences}; do not shadow the provided tools object with a local variable. A successful read_file returns text in result.observation.output. Check observation.kind for every inner call before using its output, and report failed paths rather than guessing their contents.
For a finite read-only audit, list every relevant implementation and test path in the first program and read each path once. Return answer-ready {rows, unresolved}: each row contains the requested facts and only their supporting evidence; unresolved names missing fields or failed paths. Keep the JSON-safe return below 64 KiB, normally a few kilobytes. Do not return full files, raw observations, every regex hit, or mere file counts. If unresolved is empty, answer from rows without another tool call. Otherwise follow up only on the named gaps, never on the entire file set again.
For source citations, compute 1-based line numbers from the returned text and attach {path, line, text} to each fact. Copy these triples exactly into the final answer; do not reconstruct line numbers or text from memory. A numeric limit without matching source evidence is unknown. When read_file is authorized, for example: const paths=["src/a.ts","src/b.ts"]; const rows=[],unresolved=[]; for (const path of paths) { const result=await tools.read_file({path}); if (result.observation.kind!=="success") { unresolved.push({path,error:result.observation.kind}); continue; } const evidence=result.observation.output.split("\n").flatMap((text,i)=>/^\s*isReadOnly:\s*(true|false),?\s*$/.test(text)?[{path,line:i+1,text}]:[]); if (evidence.length!==1) { unresolved.push({path,field:"isReadOnly"}); continue; } rows.push({path,isReadOnly:evidence[0].text.includes("true"),evidence}); } return {rows,unresolved};
A program call does not grant its inner tools permission.
